    "introduction": "Damaged presserfoot? It is easy to replace and this guide will take you through the necessary steps.",
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Presserfoot",
            "text": "Make sure the presser foot is in the up position.\nThe switch should be up, not in the vertical position.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/WgB1VcCrIEtJfHUY.medium",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22764/59614",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Adjust the needle to the top of its stroke using the hand wheel.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LMPecIj3xOUsePT4.medium",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22764/59618",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Lift the arm on the back of the presser foot assembly to release the foot.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22764/59615",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the presser foot.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/22764/59617",
            "comment_links": []
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": {
        "text": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
        "author_points": 30,
